    <section
      class="_section_9bee24"
      id="features"
    >
      <div
        class="_container_9bee24"
      >
        <h2
          class="_heading_9bee24"
        >
          Why Lychee
        </h2>
        <div
          class="_grid_9bee24"
        >
          <article
            class="_card_c81049"
          >
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="_icon_c81049"
            >
              ⚖️
            </span>
            <h3
              class="_title_c81049"
            >
              Smart Model Tiering
            </h3>
            <p
              class="_body_c81049"
            >
              Trivial PRs go to Haiku. Standard reviews use Sonnet. Diffs over 100,000 characters escalate automatically to Opus. Scope rules let you pin specific paths or PR labels to a different model — terraform changes can always get Opus, docs PRs can always get Haiku.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article
            class="_card_c81049"
          >
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="_icon_c81049"
            >
              🔕
            </span>
            <h3
              class="_title_c81049"
            >
              No-Spam Ergonomics
            </h3>
            <p
              class="_body_c81049"
            >
              Every PR gets one review comment, identified by a hidden HTML marker. When new commits arrive, Lychee finds and updates that comment in place — no new notifications, no duplicate threads. Inline findings are fingerprinted (SHA-256) so they are never posted twice across pushes.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article
            class="_card_c81049"
          >
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="_icon_c81049"
            >
              💰
            </span>
            <h3
              class="_title_c81049"
            >
              Predictable Cost
            </h3>
            <p
              class="_body_c81049"
            >
              Every review reports its exact token usage and USD cost in the comment footer. Set a \`budget_cap_usd\` in \`.lychee.yml\` and Lychee will halt and report a partial result rather than exceeding it. No surprise bills.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article
            class="_card_c81049"
          >
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="_icon_c81049"
            >
              🗂️
            </span>
            <h3
              class="_title_c81049"
            >
              Map-Reduce for Large PRs
            </h3>
            <p
              class="_body_c81049"
            >
              PRs exceeding 50 changed files don't get skipped or truncated. Lychee partitions them into groups of 10, reviews each group separately, then merges the results into one coherent review. The output contract is identical regardless of PR size.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article
            class="_card_c81049"
          >
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="_icon_c81049"
            >
              💬
            </span>
            <h3
              class="_title_c81049"
            >
              Interactive Commands
            </h3>
            <p
              class="_body_c81049"
            >
              Drop \`@lychee peel\` in any PR comment for a full on-demand review. \`@lychee juice\` for just the summary. \`@lychee pit\` for the single most critical finding. \`@lychee ripe?\` for the merge-readiness verdict. Commands respect the same config as automatic reviews and support an allow-list for access control.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
