                           — 
                          <code
                            class="_inlineCode_74f609"
                          >
                            update_status()
                          </code>
                           accepts any target status without validating the transition. A 
                          <code
                            class="_inlineCode_74f609"
                          >
                            completed
                          </code>
                           order can be moved back to 
                          <code
                            class="_inlineCode_74f609"
                          >
                            pending
                          </code>
                          , which may cause double-fulfillment.
                        </td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td
                          class="_severityCell_74f609 _severityminor_74f609"
                        >
                          🟡
                           
                          minor
                        </td>
                        <td>
                          tests
                        </td>
                        <td>
                          <code
                            class="_inlineCode_74f609"
                          >
                            test_stripe_webhook.py
                          </code>
                           — No test for an invalid or missing 
                          <code
                            class="_inlineCode_74f609"
                          >
                            Stripe-Signature
                          </code>
                           header. Add a test confirming a 
                          <code
                            class="_inlineCode_74f609"
                          >
                            400
                          </code>
                           response and no database write on bad signatures.
                        </td>
                      </tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
                <span
                  class="_annotation_74f609"
                >
                  Pits — findings with severity & category
                </span>
              </div>
              <div
                class="_annotatable_74f609"
                data-annotate="footer"
              >
                <div
                  class="_monospaceText_74f609"
                >
                  Tokens: 4,821 in · 612 out · $0.023  ·  Reviewed to the core by Lychee 🌴
                  <br />
                  &lt;!-- lychee:state {"last_reviewed_sha": "a3f9c12"} --&gt;
                </div>
                <span
                  class="_annotation_74f609"
                >
                  Cost footer — exact token usage and USD cost
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p
            class="_closingParagraph_74f609"
          >
            Every Lychee review follows this structure — always one comment, always updated in place, always the same shape regardless of PR size. Severity levels: 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              info
            </code>
            , 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              minor
            </code>
            , 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              major
            </code>
            , 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              critical
            </code>
            . Categories: 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              correctness
            </code>
            , 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              security
            </code>
            , 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              performance
            </code>
            , 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              tests
            </code>
            , 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              style
            </code>
            , 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              docs
            </code>
            , 
            <code
              class="_inlineCode_74f609"
            >
              other
            </code>
            . See the 
            <a
              href="/docs/glossary"
            >
              Glossary
            </a>
             for the full vocabulary.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <div
    class="_reveal_b94b86 "
  >
    <section
      class="_section_947488"
      id="commands"
    >
      <div
        class="_container_947488"
      >
        <h2
          class="_heading_947488"
        >
          Interactive Commands
        </h2>
        <div
          class="_tableWrapper_947488"
        >
          <table
            class="_table_947488"
          >
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th
                  scope="col"
                >
                  Comment
                </th>
                <th
                  scope="col"
                >
                  What it posts
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <code
                    class="_code_947488"
                  >
                    @lychee peel
                  </code>
                </td>
                <td>
                  Full review: Nectar + The Peel + Pits (same as automatic review)
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <code
                    class="_code_947488"
                  >
                    @lychee juice
                  </code>
                </td>
                <td>
                  Nectar section only — the short summary paragraph
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <code
                    class="_code_947488"
                  >
                    @lychee pit
                  </code>
                </td>
                <td>
                  The single highest-severity finding only
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <code
                    class="_code_947488"
                  >
                    @lychee ripe?
                  </code>
                </td>
                <td>
                  Ripeness verdict only — 🟢 Ripe, 🟡 Unripe, or 🔴 Sour
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p
          class="_description_947488"
        >
          Commands respect all the same configuration as automatic reviews: 
          <code>
            severity_threshold
          </code>
          , 
          <code>
            tone
          </code>
          , 
          <code>
            scope_rules
          </code>
          , 
          <code>
            inline_comments
          </code>
          , and 
          <code>
            cost_footer
          </code>
           all apply. Access can be restricted to specific GitHub logins via 
          <code>
            authorization.allowed_users
          </code>
           in 
          <code>
            .lychee.yml
          </code>
          . Unknown commands receive a help message listing all four.
        </p>
        <p
          class="_snippetTitle_947488"
        >
          Enable commands by adding to .lychee.yml:
        </p>
        <div
          class="_codeBlockWrapper_947488"
        >
          <div
            data-testid="code-block-mock"
          >
            CodeBlock Mock
          </div>
        </div>
        <a
          class="_cta_947488"
          href="/docs/commands"
        >
          Full command reference →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
